{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00346",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 6.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Doctor, hello, I've got my papers here, where should I put them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.31,
      "end_seconds": 11.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.03,
      "end_seconds": 22.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling anxious most of the day, doctor. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.59,
      "end_seconds": 25.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Okay, when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.92,
      "end_seconds": 28.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "It's been about four days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.52,
      "end_seconds": 36.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Mm. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.33,
      "end_seconds": 44.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly. Work and crowded places definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.6,
      "end_seconds": 48.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Alright, one moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.26,
      "end_seconds": 50.1,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.82,
      "end_seconds": 63.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Any thoughts of harming myself or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.82,
      "end_seconds": 66.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.16,
      "end_seconds": 70.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Has there been any chest pain on exertion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.71,
      "end_seconds": 74.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any chest pain on exertion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.33,
      "end_seconds": 81.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.39,
      "end_seconds": 95.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.67,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.96,
      "end_seconds": 99.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.66,
      "end_seconds": 103.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.25,
      "end_seconds": 106.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.24,
      "end_seconds": 109.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.72,
      "end_seconds": 121.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.43,
      "end_seconds": 124.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.13,
      "end_seconds": 127.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.38,
      "end_seconds": 129.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "No, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.04,
      "end_seconds": 134.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.43,
      "end_seconds": 136.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.95,
      "end_seconds": 155.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.44,
      "end_seconds": 158.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "No, I've never had anything serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.22,
      "end_seconds": 176.27,
      "duration_seconds": 16.05,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.91,
      "end_seconds": 178.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.97,
      "end_seconds": 183.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.75,
      "end_seconds": 186.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.88,
      "end_seconds": 208.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Pulse is regular and you're breathing comfortably right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.72,
      "end_seconds": 225.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.86,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. From what you've told me and what I found, my working impression is an anxiety disorder. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.4,
      "end_seconds": 231.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.46,
      "end_seconds": 251.98,
      "duration_seconds": 19.52,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an anxiety disorder, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling anxious most of the day for about four days, mild, and no thoughts of harming myself or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.92,
      "end_seconds": 256.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.48,
      "end_seconds": 260.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "So, are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.74,
      "end_seconds": 265.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.53,
      "end_seconds": 272.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ECG for palpitations. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.09,
      "end_seconds": 276.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.25,
      "end_seconds": 287.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "I'm prescribing escitalopram, 5 milligrams, once a day, for two weeks then review. That should help with anxiety. Regular exercise and less caffeine make a real difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.76,
      "end_seconds": 300.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.3,
      "text": "Right. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. If you have thoughts of harming yourself, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.11,
      "end_seconds": 301.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.28,
      "end_seconds": 309.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Come back in four weeks. Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.37,
      "end_seconds": 318.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "So, I take the escitalopram, 5 milligrams, once a day and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.06,
      "end_seconds": 325.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.96,
      "end_seconds": 330.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Um, no, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.26,
      "end_seconds": 333.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}